Z||000000||Formula||12-15-2001||03:04 PM||||My Formula completly broke the inside ring around the flexplate.  All bolts are still in it, it just snapped it...(in a perfect circle)<P>anyone seen this before? <P>I guess that means it has enough torque.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Untitled-1_copy.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||dgroves||12-15-2001||05:57 PM||||Had that happen on a Chevy P/U once. It was because the flexplate was not true. The real bad news was that the wobble took out the tranny pump which took out the rest of the tranny. Damn the luck||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||12-15-2001||07:01 PM||||Had it happen on a Pontiac Ventura. Harmonic balancer went out, guess it transmitted vibes back, cause the flex plate broke after a few weeks, about like you describe. I ended up with nearly 200K miles on that car tho. The external oil pump was a nice feature tho.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTDude||12-17-2001||08:41 AM||||Yeah, unfortunately it's not an uncommon problem.  Has nothing to do with horsepower or torque.  Most of the time has nothing to do with anything except a defective part.  Most of the time they start with a small crack and engine and trans vibration cause it to crack more and more. Makes one hell of a noise doesn't it.........LOL.  Just replace it and get on with life....Merry Christmas.<P>Phil Pettus<P><P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
